Of the 200 students in a school, at least 45% attended the prom night and at least 35% took part in the debating session. What is the maximum number of students who could have neither attended the prom night nor the debating session? Answer Choices: (A) 27 (B) 81 (C) 90 (D) 99 (E) 110
The number of students who attended the prom is 200 * 0.45 = 90. The number of students who took part in the debating session is 200 * 0.35 = 70. The number of students who did at least one is 90 + 70 = 160. The number of students who did not is 200 - 160 = 40. The answer is (A) 27.
Therefore, among A through E, the answer is \textbf{A}

A company produces 420 units of a particular computer component every month, at a production cost to the company of $110 per component, and sells all of the components by the end of each month. What is the minimum selling price per component that will guarantee that the yearly profit (revenue from sales minus production costs) will be at least $626,400 ? Answer Choices: (A) 226 (B) 230 (C) 240 (D) 260 (E) 280
The company produces 12 * 420 = 5040 components in a year. The minimum selling price will be the production cost plus the year's profit, divided by the number of components. 110 + 626,400 / 5040 = 110 + 124 = 234. The answer is (B) 230.
Therefore, among A through E, the answer is \textbf{B}

At a certain factory, 10 percent of the staplers produced on Monday were defective and 2 percent of the non-defective staplers were rejected by mistake. If 72 of the non-defective staplers were rejected, what was the number of staplers produced that day? Answer Choices: (A) 4,000 (B) 4,200 (C) 4,500 (D) 4,800 (E) 5,000
2 percent of the non-defective staplers were 72. So the number of non-defective is 72 / 2 * 100 = 3600. 10 percent of the staplers were defected. So the number of all is 3600 / 90 * 100 = 4000. The answer is (A).
