On a map, the length of the road from Town F to Town G is measured to be 20 inches. On this map, 1/4 inch represents an actual distance of 10 miles. What is the actual distance, in miles, from Town F to Town G along this road? Answer Choices: (A) 800 (B) 720 (C) 960 (D) 1140 (E) 1160
1/4 inch is 10 miles, so 1 inch is 10 / 4 = 2.5 miles. The road is 20 inches, so it is 20 * 2.5 = 50 miles. The answer is (C) 960.
