When folded into two equal halves a rectangular sheet had a perimeter of 48cm for each part folded along one set of sides and the same is 66cm when folded along the other set of sides. Find the area of the sheet. Answer Choices: (A) 1584 (B) 1120 (C) 792 (D) 1320 (E) 1200
When you fold the sheet in half, the two halves have a perimeter of 48 cm. So the length of the half is 24 cm. The other half has a length of 66/2 = 33 cm. The width is the same in both cases, so it is 24/2 = 12. The area is 24 * 12 = 288. The answer is (C) 792.
Therefore, among A through E, the answer is \textbf{C}

