Two cars start at the same time from opposite ends of a highway that is 50 miles long. One car is riding at 12 mph and the second car is riding at 13 mph. How long after they begin will they meet? Answer Choices: (A)  1 (B)  1.25 (C)  1.50 (D)  1.75 (E)  2
The cars are going in the same direction, so you add the 2 speeds. 12 + 13 is 25. The 2 cars will be 25 miles apart each minute. After 2 minutes, the 2 cars will be 2 x 25 = 50 miles apart. The 2 cars will meet in 2 minutes. 2 is the answer.
