In a class, 8% of total students are interested in Football. 4/5 of total students are interested in Cricket. 10% of total students are interested in Basketball and remaining 20 students are not interested in any games. How many students are there in the class? Answer Choices: (A) 850 (B) 800 (C) 900 (D) 950 (E) 1000
Let's say the total number of students is x. 8% of the students are interested in football, so 0.08x. 4/5 of the students are interested in cricket, so 0.8x. 10% of the students are interested in basketball, so 0.1x. The rest are not interested in any, so 20. x - 0.08x - 0.8x - 0.1x = 20 0.02x = 20 x = 1000 The answer is (E) 1000.
